files_under uses p.rglob and x.is_file(). is_file follows a symlink, so a symlink to a file is listed as if it were a file in the tree. The target can sit outside the directory.

Skip symlinks. Do not open them and do not list them. A regular file is still listed.

Replace files_under with:

def files_under(p: Path) -> list[str]:
    if not p.is_dir() or p.is_symlink():
        return []
    names = []
    for path in p.rglob("*"):
        if path.is_symlink():
            continue
        if path.is_file():
            names.append(str(path.relative_to(p)))
    return sorted(names)

